Hello, crusaders! 

An update 2.7.0W for PC and PS4/Xbox Series X/S is here! 

[b]Highlights:[/b]
[list]
[*] Now you can enjoy the music from Skar Productions in the "Credits" tab. The track is only available for those who have finished the game at least once to avoid spoilers.
[*] Brazilian Portuguese and Italian based on community localizations have been added to the main game on consoles.
[/list]
[previewyoutube=zaoWUUDQq8M;full][/previewyoutube]
[b]Beware of possible plot spoilers below![/b]
[b]Areas[/b]
[list]
[*] Companions could jump onto the roof of the Wintersun leader's house when leaving the room to go outside — fixed; 
[*] Fixed a bug in Drezen causing the passage for the mythic path of the Swarm to be blocked if he absorbed a Gesmerha in the throne room;
[*] If Daeran was killed under certain circumstances, his body could stay in the Commander's chambers forever — fixed.
[/list]
[b]Items[/b]
[list]
[*] Barding of Tenacity for your horse now correctly have +3 enchantment;
[*] Heavy shields +3 is now correctly named, given the bonus; 
[*] Mighty Blow Of Good weapon now deals the correct damage; 
[*] Teleport ability by Cape of Morta could be used in restricted areas — fixed. Teleportation now properly works in restricted areas;
[*] The Acts of Iomedae book now stands out more clearly in the inventory.
[/list]
[b]Crusade[/b]
[list]
[*] Alchemist now deal fire damage with their bombs instead of ice and can shoot with crossbows;
[*] Beer elementals now deal more damage;
[*] Summoned wolves now deal more damage;
[*] Water elementals now deal more damage with attacks and spells.
[/list]
[b]Classes & Mechanics[/b]
[list]
[*] Bloodseeker now correclty loses Bloodlust bonunes when changing the archetype; 
[*] Focused Strike feat no longer avialiable for animal companions;
[*] Magic Deceiver could add spells from Draconic bloodline to the spellbook when taking Dragon Disciple prestige class — fixed; 
[*] Primalist progression at level 4 now works correctly; 
[*] Sorcerous Claws now work and show up correctly.
[/list]
[b]UI[/b]
[list]
[*] Fixed a bug where a player could lose the option to reveal the menu for using consumable items (potions and scrolls) in his inventory after a battle;
[*] Fixed the descriptions and tags for Cleric domains: Animal, Earth, Undead, Evil, Liberation, Madness, Scalykind, Weather;
[*] Fixed the screenshot preview of a tavern group photo in A Dance of Masks DLC.
[*] 
[/list]
[b]Visual[/b]
[list]
[*] Added animations for Seelah when she tries to get Anevia from under the rocks in the Kenabres сaves;
[*] Improved the cutscene of the minotaur's appearance during the battle for Defender's Heart.
[/list]
[b]Misс[/b]
[list]
[*] Fixed a bug in rider and mount movement when using the cursor.
[*] Fixed reactivity on Apsu and Dahak's religion in dialogue with Lathimas;
[*] If a character was riding a mount when transitioning from the global map, they could start flashing or become invisible — fixed; 
[*] In some dialogues, after the player selected unique answer options for Apsu or Dahak's follower, the protagonist did not receive any bonuses — fixed. Selecting these options in dialogue will now result in a temporary buff;
[*] Updated and corrected information in the "Credits" tab;
[*] Now you can enjoy the music from Skar Production in the "Credits" tab. The track is only available for those who have finished the game at least once to avoid spoilers;  
[*] Multiple text fixes to descriptions and abilities.
[/list]

Hello, crusaders! 

An update 2.5.0y is here! 

[b]Highlights:[/b]
[list]
[*] The Gold Dragon mythic path has spread its wings: multiple mechanical improvements, visual updates, 2 new dragon-themed religions - Apsu and Dahak, the ability to turn some characters' lives towards redemption and more!
[/list]
More info: https://store.steampowered.com/news/app/1184370/view/6564653885911203913

If you are playing with mods, don’t forget to update them before loading your saves! Old version 2.4.1i will remain available via the beta tab in Steam for mod users.

[b]Beware of possible plot spoilers below![/b]

[b]Areas[/b]
[list]
[*] A party from The Lord of Nothing DLC appeared in Drezen's Tavern even if the player followed the Swarm Mythic Path — fixed; 
[*] Fixed an issue that could cause the rest on Azata Island to break;
[*] Fixed incorrect completion of the Dance of Masks DLC for Swarm-that-Walks. Previously, players after visiting Razmir could get to the Kenabres square and get stuck. Now, players will be transported to the global map as they should have been;
[*] Players that were left in the square without being able to leave it will be transferred to the global map as soon as they load the save. Also, player characters that mistakenly entered the arena through the square will be transferred to the global map;
[*] Fixed the gathering of Crusader supplies for a full rest during the siege of Drezen;
[*] In Areelu's Laboratory in the Chapter 5, attempting the stairs (accessed with the Crystal Key item) will now carry the entire party to its beginning, rather than one participant at a time;
[*] Miammir did not come to Drezen in chapter 5 — fixed;
[*] Ramien  did not come to Drezen in chapter 5 — fixed;
[*] Ramien could stand in the camp in the Threshold even for the Swarm that Walks mythic path  — fixed;
[*] The crusaders appeared in the Threshold even if the player have chosen the Swarm That Walked Mythic Path — fixed;
[*] The dialogues in Drezen with Chun Dawei, Hulrun, Nystra, Ciar and Klaem in Chapter 5 were not showing correctly — fixed; 
[*] The Inheritor' Hand is no longer located in the Ivory Sanctum after being encountered in Drezen;
[*] The passage to the secret room on one of the islands in The Treasure of the Midnight Isles DLC did not appear — fixed;
[*] When killing the boss Drimo in the arena in A Dance of Masks DLC by a character under the effect of Phoenix Gift, the character does not die from the curse and further passage of the arena is blocked — fixed; 
[*] You can now attempt to leave the dialogue with two oreads troubled with picking flags for the festival in A Dance of Masks DLC;
[*] After talking to Greybor in Drezen's Tavern in the Chapter 3 and hiring him into the team, the wrong dialogue was playing — fixed.
[/list]
[b]Quests[/b]
[list]
[*] Anevia disappeared after leaving the basement in Drezen, where the commander was called by Camellia, and it was impossible to complete the quest — fixed;
[*] Fixed the opportunity to take a quest from Gverm if the player kicked out Camellia, who was needed for the quest;
[*] Fye the Tavern Keeper would show up at the tavern even if he had previously been sent to jail — fixed; 
[*] Nocticula no longer interrupts dialog during the quest with Sosiel's brother.
[/list]
[b]Items[/b]
[list]
[*] Gloves of Neophyte didn't work with Ignition spell - fixed;
[*] Ring of sharp strike didn't work correctly - fixed.
[/list]
[b]Crusade[/b]
[list]
[*] Ash Giants become more dangerous.
[/list]
[b]Classes & Mechanics[/b]
[list]
[*] There have been some changes to the Faceless Sphinx encounter:
1) We've made Areshkagal stop disguising herself as a super-powered sphinx, and now her primary class is an outsider;
2) By sacrificing to cosmic entities, we've also managed to weaken the Faceless Sphinx's body somewhat (however, many of us paid for this with our lives and sanity);
3) Despite all our efforts (or because of them), Areshkagal now correctly creates copies of herself in the first phase of the encounter with her;
4) The abilities and behavior of elemental Areshkagal in the third encounter phase have been significantly improved;
5) Now you only need to use Midnight Bolt to drop a Nahyndrian Crystal for the secret ending on the last surviving Areshkagal in the third encounter phase;
[*] Arcane bond now works correctly; 
[*] Bloodseeker's Enervation spell now works correctly and imposes negative levels; 
[*] Defeating ghosts in the Visitors from Morta DLC granted the wrong amount of experience - fixed;
[*] Edge of Force and Explosive Runes now work correctly; 
[*] Enveloping Winds prerequisite for Aerial Evasion didn't work correctly — fixed; 
[*] Expose Vulnerability ability now works correctly; 
[*] Fixed lava damage on low health on low difficulty levels;
[*] Fixed the difficulty display for saving throws from a flock of dead crows in the Carrion Storm ability;
[*] Fixed the logic of applying the “Commander's Banner” effect; now it is applied correctly, and also does not apply if the banner was lost;
[*] Hellknight Signifer now removes armor speed penalty on 3-rd level instead of 8-th;
[*] Oracle  Flame Curse now removes armor speed penalty on 10-th level instead of 1-th;
[*] Warpriest Aspect of War now correctly removes armor and encumbrance speed penalties;
[*] Inciter's (Skald archetype) "Hit a Nerve" ability now correctly removes the armor penalty if the character has the "Mythic Inspiration" mythic ability;
[*] Kitsune in a human form could bite — fixed; 
[*] Mythic Armor Focus (Light Armor) — Endurance now correctly shows the spell resistance; 
[*] Mythic Armor Focus (Medium Armor) — Assault feat now deals piercing damage instead of slashing;
[*] Now the Divine Hunter who chose the Animal domain at level 1 can correctly choose bonuses to the characteristics of his animal companion;
[*] Sense Vitals spell was displayed twice in the Wizard spellbook;
[*] Spindle infusion had wrong costs which resulted in inability to use it with advanced blasts in some cases — fixed;
[*] The Bound of Possibility cloak now doesn't give a penalty to the Trickster; 
[*] The entire party will now receive the “Commander's Banner” effect when leaving the Areelu's Lab, not just the player character;
[*] The Greedy Mystic Spell Eater (a little dragon summoned by the Arcane Undertow of the Midnight Islands) ate too little, causing its stats to drop. We fixed it, and little fellow is now functioning correctly;
[*] The Prophet of Pestilence's Thousand Diseases ability now has the correct saving throw DC;
[*] The Spirit Naga form granted by the Sorcerer's Serpentine Bloodline now has the correct venom saving throw DC and bite damage;
[*] Tortured crusader could keep Alone in the Dark ability after respec — fixed; 
[*] Tortured Crusader's bonus attack from the Unbroken Paragon  ability was giving the wrong attack bonus — fixed;
[*] Magic Nullification mythic ability now correctly makes the character immune to magic.
[/list]
[b]UI[/b]
[list]
[*] Added prerequisite for Spell Specialization Feat;
[*] It was impossible to spend a skillpoint into Intelligence for the Animal Companion — fixed; 
[*] Nahyndrian crystal was displayed in the interface without the important item frame - fixed;
[*] Now you can choose the Vordakai portrait for the Lich path.
[/list]
[b]Visual[/b]
[list]
[*] Characters from The Lord of Nothing DLC appeared with a delay in the tavern cutscene in A Dance of the Masks DLC — fixed; 
[*] Mythical weather in Drezen was being replaced with common weather after skipping time — fixed; 
[*] The dwarf lady in Storasta in The Lord of Nothing DLC now has a correct modeling instead of a human.
[/list]
[b]System[/b]
[list]
[*] The game crashed when moving to another location if there was a character in the party who died with an active “Disintegrate” effect — fixed;
[*] The game was freezing when trying to load Drezen after completing A Dance of Masks DLC — fixed.
[/list]
[b]Misс[/b]
[list]
[*] Valestry, Master of Steps in Razmir's Palace has remembered his own name;
[*] Yaker could visit the Commander for a conversation involving Regill, even though Regill is excluded from the companion roster — fixed;
[*] Dialogue with the tentacles-hating aasimar's squires broke when repeatedly refusing to help them, but then changing your mind. We fixed everything, tentacles be praised.
[/list]

Hello, crusaders! 

An update 2.4.1i is here!

[b]Highlights:[/b]
[list]
[*] We've fixed several bugs that prevented you from starting or completing the Visitors from Morta DLC! 
[*] Improved navigation in many locations of the game — say no to falling off the map and getting stuck in level geometry;
[*] The interface will no longer freeze when clicking on a character's portrait!
[/list]
If you are playing with mods, don’t forget to update them before loading your saves! 

Beware of possible plot spoilers below!

[b]Areas[/b]
[list]
[*] Capitan Seilkind could disappear in the Mineshaft Fourteen — fixed;
[*] The empty hall of the Gray Garrison on the mythic path of Legend is no longer empty;
[*] Improved navigation in many locations in the game;
[*] Fixed a bug where it was impossible to kill a vampire in the coffin in the Ivory Sanctum. Now you can kill it safely and get the item “Phantom Slayer's Bracers” from it. The change will take effect only for those players who have not yet visited the Ivory Sanctum;
[/list]
[b]Quests[/b]
[list]
[*] The dialogue in Woljif's personal quest in the third chapter could play incorrectly if Woljif died — fixed;
[*] Arsinoe claimed to have marked the location “Morbid Ridge” on the map, but did not actually do so — fixed;
[*] Yaker will now not come to report to the Сommander unless Regill has been accepted as a companion;
[*] The dialogue with Lucy and John in the location “Morbid Ridge” could start again after the characters go back to their world — fixed;
[*] In the “Lord of Nothing” DLC, the game could incorrectly read a companion's state, confusing whether or not they survived the ritual — fixed;
[*] Seelah could die in battle during her personal quest — fixed;
[*] The quest “The Last Gift of a Brilliant Mind” is no longer marked as mandatory in chapter three;
[*] If the party did not include Lann or Ember, the dialog with goblins in the Visitors from Morta DLC could break the quest — fixed;
[/list]
[b]Classes & Mechanics[/b]
[list]
[*] Sometimes it was impossible to get the “Commander's Banner” effect after Iz and the subsequent story scene in Drezen — fixed;
[*] Fixed a bug where you could get the “Commander's Banner” effect in Alushinirra and the arena from the “Dance of the Masks” DLC. The change will only apply from a new game on;
[*] Paladins no longer can select Achaekek as their deity;
[*] Fixed premature death of a companion after visiting the Razmir's palace (after returning to the festive square of Kenabres). Now companions will not be dragged away from the tavern and it will be possible to correctly complete the DLC story;
[*] Magus Independent Ego ability did not give a bonus to AC when the character held a sword in their hand — fixed;
[*] We have banned Swarm-That-Walks from hiring mercenaries even during the game expansions;
[*] The trap in the Grey Garrison now only triggers on companions of the player character. No more companions will die because a non—player character accidentally stepped on the trap;
[*] Changed the way Blood Boil spell works in Verdant Caves in The Lord of Nothing DLC. Now it will be properly removed after battle;
[*] If you click on a forbidden deity when creating a character with the deceiver archetype, all previously selected character generation steps will “reset” and subclasses that require no deity will be blocked or turned red — fixed;
[*] Fixed giving Commander's Banner buff to the whole party when moving to the 3rd chapter. Now the buff is issued correctly, according to the description;
[/list]
[b]UI[/b]
[list]
[*] Irabeth's portrait did not change after a certain dialog with the player character, although it should have — fixed;
[*] The interface will no longer freeze when clicking on a character's portrait;
[*] Fixed the inability to move the player character on the global map when the tutorial window is active with an active gamepad; 
[/list]
[b]Visual[/b]
[list]
[*] Fixed the cutscene with Arushalaie in Areelu's lab;
[*] One of the animations in Nenio's final personal quest was playing incorrectly — fixed;
[*] The cutscene of Yozz leaving when attacking him in Drezen could freeze for a long time — fixed;
[/list]
[b]Misс[/b]
[list]
[*] In Dance of Masks DLC, while standing in line before the festival, an option to hide your identity was unavailable when interacting with two men, who recognized the Commander — fixed;
[*] Companion pets were so excited to meet Nenio for the first time that they were becoming uncontrollably chaotic — fixed;
[*] Daeran will no longer disappear during the romance cutscenes.
[/list]

Hello, crusaders! 
An update 2.4.0x is here!

[b]Highlights:[/b]
[list]
[*] Fixed bugs related to romantic companion scenes. No more lovers will run out of your chambers, nor will their abilities disappear after dates!
[*] Added new weather for different mythic paths;
[*] Numerous bug fixes related to recently added archetypes and spells;
[*] Reworked the state of Drezen city for Swarm-That-Walks and a lot of fixes for Swarm-That-Walks including a new cutscene.
[/list]
If you are playing with mods, don’t forget to update them before loading your saves! If the mods have not been updated yet and you want to play on the old version, then switch to the 2.3.3k.

[b]Beware of possible plot spoilers below![/b]

[b]Areas[/b]
[list]
[*] Mythic Demon could enter the inaccessible area of the Ineluctable Prison - fixed;
[*] Swarm-That-Walks has the counselors and crusaders removed from Drezen, and tultist traders added in place of the normal traders;
[*] Improved the navigation in Midnight Fane;
[*] Greybor will no longer appear in the tavern if he was killed by the player character;
[*] If Gesmerha was devoured by Swarm-That-Walks, she will not apear in Wintersun anymore;
[*] Ulbrig will no longer run around the camp during the gargoyle attack before meeting the Commander;
[*] Sosiel no longer runs away from the Commander's bedroom after loading a save in that location;
[*] The party can no longer go outside the map in one of the Ember quests;
[*] Nymphs will no longer mourn the burning of the tree in Storasta if they are dead;
[*] Now in all parts of Storasta the terrain type is displayed correctly;
[*] The Quasit that rewards the player in Chapter 5 can now be found using the minimap;
[*] Fixed a bug where the scene of demons torturing townspeople overlapped with the romantic scene with Camelia in the temple;
[*] Fixed a bug in Drezen where Anevia might not return to her place in the throneroom and interfere with other petitioners. Also fixed a possible delay in the event about finding the killer in Drezen;
[*] Removed an unnecessary extra key from Razmir's Palace in A Dance of Masks DLC;
[*] During the gargoyle attack on the crusaders' camp in the 2nd chapter, Ulbrig fought with his bare hands and without buffs – fixed;
[*] Fixed the navigation in Reliable Redoubt;
[*] Fixed the animation bug when the characters were leaving Garden of the Gods;
[*] Fixed the appearance of mercenaries at the celebration in A Dance of Masks DLC;
[*] A wrong island could appear in Treasure of The Midnight Isles DLC. Those who are already on this island will still be able to explore and leave it;
[*] When changing the party members in Razmir's palace, a mercenary could disappear - fixed;
[*] Improved visibility in the cutscene with the vescavor bait. Now the soldiers will not go into the darkness, the cutscene with them being absorbed by the swarm will be clearly visible;
[*] Now after visiting Areelu's laboratory, the rest on the Azata island will not be replaced by a fake one. 
[/list]
[b]Quests[/b]
[list]
[*] Added Ulbrig's cues for several occasions during the game - the Blackwater quest, Seilkind's quest, Morveg's quest, etc;
[*] Removed the option to infinitely gain alignment for Azatas in Threshold;
[*] An attack on the Defender's Heart tavern can now occur if, after being informed of readiness to assault the Gray Garrison, the player's character refused to go during the party formation stage;
[*] Now the quest "Starward Gaze" fails at the beginning of the second chapter if it was not completed in the first chapter;
[*] Fixed a bug where the hag could remain alive when choosing to kill her during the Arushalae's quest;
[*] The cutscene with Voetiel could function incorrectly when the player was using a gamepad - fixed;
[*] If the player character leaves the path of the Lich and becomes a Legend, Golden Dragon, or Swarm-That-Walks, they will have the opportunity to gather companions upon exiting the ziggurat;
[*] Reworked the skill check when trying to move the golem during the Wolzhif's quest. Now, if you fail, the player will still be able to move the golem, but it will take time, and everyone in the party will get tired;
[*] When descending into the Nexus mines, you will no longer be prompted to reform your party if the Lich has completed all of the tasks;
[*] Swarm That Walks couldn't inspect the points of interest in Kenabres in A Dance of Masks DLC – fixed;
[*] In A Dance of Masks DLC, Seelah will no longer mention the arena before you visited it;
[*] Now goblin Norte's quest will fail if you decide to attack him during the conversation near cages;
[*] Sparing the swindling actors in A Dance of Masks DLC provided too much Chaotic points to a player - fixed;
[*] Slightly reworked the romantic event with Galfrey in A Dance of Masks DLC;
[*] Now the crusaders in Sosiel's scene in the Lost Chapel will not appear if Sosiel was banished from the party;
[*] In some cases Greybor's quest in Chapter 5 didn't unlock properly — fixed;
[*] After loading an autosave made after Pulura's Fall, Hand of the Inheritor would stop interacting with the Commander - fixed;  
[*] "A Lesson in Applied Conjuration" quest didn't fail after enetring the Chapter 4 — fixed;
[*] "Middlegame" quest was mistakenly issued with automatic crusade enabled — fixed; 
[*] "Endgame" quest was mistakenly issued with automatic crusade enabled — fixed; 
[*] "Feud of the Faithful" quest didn't fail after enetring the Chapter 2 — fixed;
[*] "Demonic Parasites" quest didn't fail after enetring the Chapter 4 — fixed;
[*] If a player ate Malessa in Drezen as Swarm-That-Walks, they could still get the quest to save her — fixed.
[/list]
[b]Items[/b]
[list]
[*] Additional damage of Virtuous Starknife is cold iron now;
[*] Updated the loot in Razmir's Palace illustrated book episode;
[*] Scarab of Protection and Medallion of Demonic Disruption no longer counts as junk when autoselling;
[*] Angel's sword Speed of Light now gives two additional attacks instead of one.
[/list]
[b]Crusade[/b]
[list]
[*] Call for Reserve event used to summon different amount of units each time – fixed, now it will be more predictable;
[*] Blade of the inheritor ability was not dealing damage — fixed.
[/list]
[b]Classes & Mechanics[/b]
[list]
[*] In the third act, we added a shortcut from Lands of Yath to West Sellen for PC's party. Please note that it does not work for the armies;
[*] If Ulbrig joins in Chapter 5 and the player character is a Legend, Ulbrig will gain 8 mythic levels;
[*] When completing Chapter 2, the characters will fully heal and get rid of all negative effects;
[*] The player's character will no longer suffer from overencumbrance during Arushalae's dream;
[*] Feat "Shifter's Edge" now works correctly;
[*] Daeran can now be kicked from the party in Chapter 4;
[*] Some characters from Queen Galfrey's escort in Iz did not participate in the battle - fixed;
[*] Now in arena battles, characters will appear on their mounts;
[*] Blinding Ray now works correctly;
[*] Mythic Buckler — Flying Shield Style now works correctly;
[*] Bladebound's Black Blade had an incorrect number of HP – fixed;
[*] The intoxication from a Fermented Beer Elemental was so strong, that it could damage the fabric of reality itself, causing the game to crash. We've reduced its strength, and now you can enjoy both the beer and the game. For the glory of Cayden Cailean!
[*] Arcane Bond didn't replenish spell slots for sorcerers – fixed;
[*] Some classes, like monks, could't take levels in Living Grimoire archetype – fixed;
[*] Fixed an issue with kinetic blade, which prevented characters from making an attack of opportunity;
[*] Loremaster didn't get benefits from selecting Living Grimoire's spellbook – fixed;
[*] Changed the way Blood Boil spell works in Verdant Caves in The Lord of Nothing DLC. Now it will be properly removed after battle;
[*] Kinetic Knight's Kinetic Warrior ability now counts as having Combat Expertise for Feint;
[*] Magic Deceiver – Living Deity can now have 4 domains with Trickster's Lore (Religion) 2 rank;
[*] Proclaimer's abilities disappeared at the 19th level instead of upgrading – fixed;
[*] Sable Company Marine's hippogriff companion didn't get favored enemy bonuses – fixed;
[*] Thassilonian Specialist can select spells from DLCs now;
[*] Holding Living Grimoire's holy book erroneously activated warpriest's Sacred Weapon ability for the weapon selected for Weapon Focus feat – fixed;
[*] After being used on dominated allies, the Deadly Fascination ability of the Mantis Zealot archetype didn't stop working after the domination effect ended – fixed;
[*] Pestilence Spirit, the unique spirit of Prophet of Pestilence shaman archetype, has received its own manifestation;
[*] Reworked the progression of Bladebound magus archetype. True Magus feat has been replaced with a brand new True Bond feat. Independent Ego ability now provides an AC bonus, when the bladehound is holding their black blade;
[*] Clarified the description of prerequisites for warpriest's bonus feats, added information about the BAB;
[*] Some enchantmets of Living Grimoire's holy book didn't work correctly – fixed;
[*] Spell Bane feat didn't work with Bane special ability of Living Grimoire's holy book – fixed;
[*] Kinetic Sharpshooter is now proficient with all shields except Tower Shields, and got a new unique 20 level feat;
[*] The Spell Master's (Mage archetype) ability "Focused Spells" now functions correctly;
[*] Mounted characters will now also move to the starting positions at the end of the battle;
[*] Warpriest archetype's Red Shroud ability, Mantis Zealot sub-class, at level 13 is used via a quick action instead of a free one - fixed;
[*] Features that buff the cavalier when they perform a Charge attack will now correctly buff them if the attack was initiated by a pet;
[*] Guarded Hearth ability has returned to the previous version of bonus types - fixed;
[*] Bloodseeker's Sense Vitals ability was calculated incorrectly - fixed;
[*] Fixed a bug where Wenduag could lose the ability to shift after one of the romantic events;
[*] Barbarian's Rage Power Come and Get Me is now correctly issued if you first enable the rage power ability and then use rage;
[*] The hippogriff's Flying Attack ability didn't work correctly against swarm-type enemies - fixed;
[*] Fixed Paladin's mount progression;
[*] Fixed Devil/Demon aspects not working for fiendflesh shifter on level 9;
[*] Fixed the lacking buff when the player is resting on the island of Azata;
[*] Devil's decree of Never-ending War didn't work - fixed;
[*] Fixed the damage description of the Exploding Arrows infusion of the Kinetic Sharpshooter archetype;  
[*] Imitator's Master Slayer ability requirements were reworked for it to work correctly;
[*] Bloodseekr archetype has been reworked and got a lot of new abilities: 1) All blood abilities that required a save throw got a difficulty boost. Now the formula is 10+ Bloodseeker level + Intelligence mod. 2) Blood Jet ability - damage increased to 1d8 per Bloodseeker level. 3) Cone of Blood ability - damage increased to 1d6 per Bloodseeker level. 4) Carrion Form ability - now has undead feats. 5) Master of Blood ability - now the same reinforcement bonuses are given to spells for blood points - Enervation, Wracking Ray, Vampiric Shadow Shield, Vampiric Touch. Also changed the descriptor type from Profane to Inherent. 6) Added a new ability - Growing Thirst (levels 4,8,12,16) - increases the crit range of Bloodseeker's bite by 1.
[/list]
[b]UI[/b]
[list]
[*] Fixed an incorrect description of the action at the Rasping Rifts location;
[*] During the dialogue with Nocticula, Iomedae's lines appeared with the wrong portrait - fixed;
[*] The description of the "Shatter Ceiling" ability in the Purple Worm's ability has been fixed;
[*] Fixed dialogue during the personal quest of the Seelah when playing as Aeon;
[*] Improved the display of some text messages when exploring the festival square of Kenabres;
[*] Sometimes after a romantic scene in the bedroom, an icon on the door could disappear, making it difficult to exit the room – fixed;
[*] Fixed a number of typos and "unknown key" errors in descriptions;
[*] The Sable Company Marine archetype now has the Hippogriff's Flying Attack ability on the quick access bar;
[*] Fixed Anevia's wrong conversation line.
[/list]
[b]Visual[/b]
[list]
[*] The halo of the Angel or the swarm of insects of Swarm-That-Walks was located on the character model lower than intended - fixed;
[*] Fixed visual effects of demons spawning in some locations;
[*] Fixed Staunton's animations in conversation after returning from the past in the Aeon storyline;
[*] We asked the dragons to move over during the cutscene in Threshhold, and now there's enough room for everyone;
[*] Fixed incorrect lighting in Nameless Ruins;
[*] Ulbrig now removes his griffon form during the first encounter with Sigvorn and Ysenna;
[*] Improved dialogue cutscene in Blackwing Library;
[*] Fixed a visual bug where the cavallier would put their weapon away after attacking;
[*] Fixed the visual effect of inquisitor's Word of God ability;
[*] After shifting back to humanoid form, a shifter character could experience issues with helmet and backpack visibility settings – fixed;
[*] Fixed a number of cutscenes where characters' appearances were altered – they will return to their normal looks now;
[*] The player will now dismount during the cutscene of the first meeting with Irabeth;
[*] Fixed the limping animation;
[*] Fixed a bug where some mongrels could disappear if saves from older versions were loaded into new ones;
[*] Fixed the limping animation;
[*] Swarm-That-Walks can now eat the entire Chilly Creek village in the new cutscene, if they ate Malessa before.
[/list]
[b]System[/b]
[list]
